## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.11+
- Node.js 18+
- Gemini API Key ([Get it here](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey))

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/ai-architecture-reviewer.git
cd ai-architecture-reviewer
2️⃣ Backend Setup
bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv

# Windows
venv\Scripts\activate

# Mac/Linux
source venv/bin/activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env
# Add your GEMINI_API_KEY in .env

uvicorn main:app --reload
Backend runs at http://localhost:8000
API docs at http://localhost:8000/docs

3️⃣ Frontend Setup
Open a new terminal:

bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
Frontend runs at http://localhost:5173 🎉

📁 Project Structure
text
ai-architecture-reviewer/
├── backend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── models/          # SQLAlchemy DB models
│   │   ├── schemas/         # Pydantic schemas
│   │   ├── routers/         # API endpoints
│   │   ├── services/        # Business logic
│   │   ├── ai/              # Gemini integration
│   │   ├── graph/           # Knowledge Graph + GraphRAG
│   │   ├── static_analysis/ # AST-based code parsing
│   │   ├── vectorstore/     # ChromaDB integration
│   │   ├── core/            # Security, config
│   │   └── utils/           # Helpers
│   ├── data/                # SQLite DB, uploads, vectors
│   ├── scripts/             # DB init, seed scripts
│   └── tests/               # Unit tests
├── frontend/
│   └── src/
│       ├── api/             # Axios API calls
│       ├── components/      # Reusable UI components
│       ├── pages/           # Route pages
│       ├── hooks/           # Custom React hooks
│       ├── context/         # React contexts
│       ├── store/           # Zustand stores
│       └── utils/           # Helpers
├── database/                # SQL schema + migrations
├── docs/                    # Documentation
├── diagrams/                # Architecture diagrams
└── screenshots/             # UI screenshots
🔄 How It Works
text
1. User registers / logs in → JWT token issued
2. User creates a new project
3. User provides architecture input:
   - Text description, OR
   - Code files upload (Python/Java), OR
   - Diagram upload
4. Backend pipeline:
   a. Static Analysis  → parse code, extract dependencies
   b. Knowledge Graph  → build nodes + edges (NetworkX)
   c. GraphRAG         → embed + retrieve relevant patterns
   d. Gemini API       → detect flaws, recommend fixes, build roadmap
5. Results saved to SQLite
6. Frontend displays:
   - Dashboard with metrics + charts
   - Interactive graph (React Flow)
   - Flaw list + recommendation cards
   - Modernization roadmap timeline
   - Downloadable PDF report
